Alembic migrations (async, PostGIS-aware).

    uv run alembic upgrade head                      # apply everything
    uv run alembic downgrade -1                      # step back one
    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate --rev-id 0002 -m "add users"
    uv run alembic upgrade head --sql                # review the SQL first

Revision IDs are sequential four-digit numbers (0001, 0002, ...) assigned with
--rev-id, so migration files sort in apply order.

Two rules:

1. Read every autogenerated migration before committing it. Alembic does not
   reliably get spatial indexes, enum changes, or server defaults right, and the
   GeoAlchemy2 rewriter in env.py only covers the spatial cases it knows about.

2. Import new model modules in env.py. Autogenerate compares the database against
   Base.metadata, and metadata only contains models that have been imported —
   a model nobody imports produces an empty migration and no warning.
